It would be good if the Blessed One would explain the meaning of these words.

15
00:02:07,953 --> 00:02:08,593
Well, listen up.

16
00:02:10,075 --> 00:02:12,199
He's an Americanism, says the Buddha.

17
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:23,235
So someone who is an inquirer, not knowing how to read another person's mind, should investigate as a targeter in respect to two states.

18
00:02:23,856 --> 00:02:26,661
States cognizable through the eye and through the ear.

19
00:02:26,721 --> 00:02:32,669
In other words, watch the Tathagata and listen to what he says.

20
00:02:34,372 --> 00:02:39,980
Are there found in the Tathagata defiled states that can be recognized?

21
00:02:41,362 --> 00:02:46,991
And when he does this, he'll come to recognize that there are no defiled states in the Blessing Book.

22
00:02:49,115 --> 00:02:50,978
But then he must investigate further.

23
00:02:52,391 --> 00:03:01,881
Are they found in the Tathagata any mixed states cognizable by the eye or through the ear that they can see and hear?

24
00:03:02,681 --> 00:03:07,225
So mixed state means one minute he's the Buddha and next minute he's not.

25
00:03:07,366 --> 00:03:11,510
And in a sense, that's the way we are.

26
00:03:11,531 --> 00:03:17,355
Sometimes I'm Buddha and sometimes I'm definitely not.

27
00:03:17,376 --> 00:03:20,239
So no mixed states can be found in the Tathagata.

28
00:03:22,361 --> 00:03:26,668
Then he says you must investigate further.

29
00:03:28,210 --> 00:03:38,883
Are there found in the Tathagata or not cleansed states that you can see and upon hearing the Buddha you can hear it?

30
00:03:39,485 --> 00:03:42,788
So of course there are cleansed states, in other words virtue.

31
00:03:45,992 --> 00:03:48,657
Now when he comes to this he investigates further.

32
00:03:49,447 --> 00:03:52,389
long time or did he attain it recently?

33
00:03:52,950 --> 00:03:57,395
And the answer is the Venerable One has attained this wholesome state over a long time.

34
00:03:58,056 --> 00:04:05,544
So now this puts big question marks on people who have sudden enlightenment and go around saying that they're fully liberated.

35
00:04:06,724 --> 00:04:09,828
The 60s and 70s were full of such people, gurus.

36
00:04:11,008 --> 00:04:18,677
So in other words, the Buddha stresses here that you don't become awakened just as soon as you wake up in the morning.

37
00:04:21,391 --> 00:04:23,793
Now you must investigate further.

38
00:04:25,235 --> 00:04:36,189
Has the Venerable acquired renown and attained fame so that the dangers connected with renown and fame are found in him?

39
00:04:36,209 --> 00:04:49,524
So once somebody becomes famous, do we see any pride, any conceit, any arrogance, the abuse of power, the abuse of his students,

40
00:04:51,125 --> 00:04:54,348
No, this is not to be found in the Buddha.

41
00:04:58,572 --> 00:05:00,795
Then you must investigate further.

42
00:05:02,317 --> 00:05:15,672
Is the Venerable One restrained without fear or restrained by fear?

43
00:05:17,194 --> 00:05:21,098
Does he avoid indulging in sensual pleasure because

44
00:05:21,262 --> 00:05:25,910
He is without craving through the destruction of craving.

45
00:05:27,492 --> 00:05:28,593
That's an interesting point.

46
00:05:29,194 --> 00:05:36,105
Is he pretending to be restrained or is it because all fear has gone?

47
00:05:37,146 --> 00:05:40,170
So that's a difficult one to get at.

48
00:05:40,971 --> 00:05:42,834
You'd have to catch the person, you know.

49
00:05:46,821 --> 00:05:49,785
And not indulging in sensual pleasures.

50
00:05:50,288 --> 00:05:59,300
So, you know, because there is no more craving, there's no more craving or identifying with anything which is pleasurable.

51
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:03,884
So one has to observe carefully, one has to stay with somebody for quite some time.

52
