There's a story about Ajahn Chah who had heard about this Arahant and he went to stay with him.

53
00:06:12,757 --> 00:06:17,663
And seemingly he was with him for quite some time and

54
00:06:18,048 --> 00:06:23,574
was of the growing opinion that maybe this monk was indeed fully liberated.

55
00:06:24,295 --> 00:06:37,192
And then one day, just by happenchance, he saw him give this great dog, he saw him give this dog a great kick because the dog had sort of taken a piece of meat off the table.

56
00:06:38,035 --> 00:06:40,317
So I think he left after that.

57
00:06:44,843 --> 00:06:47,447
So he must investigate even further

58
00:06:52,252 --> 00:07:14,834
what are the venerable reasons uh sorry just a minute i've missed it here uh connection uh comes and it comes to know right that um okay so then um the other if others should ask you

59
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:17,401
What are the Venerable One's reasons?

60
00:07:18,163 --> 00:07:19,225
What are your reasons?

61
00:07:19,245 --> 00:07:27,012
And what is your evidence for saying that this Venerable One is restrained without fear, not restrained by fear?

62
00:07:27,314 --> 00:07:34,742
He avoids indulging in sensual pleasures because he is without craving and the destruction of craving.

63
00:07:35,423 --> 00:07:36,403
Then they should answer.

64
00:07:37,064 --> 00:07:40,148
Whether the Venerable One dwells in the Sangha or not,

65
00:07:40,447 --> 00:08:02,439
While some there are well-behaved and some are ill-behaved and some there teach a group, while some here are seen concerned with material things and some are unsullied by material things, still that venerable one does not despise anyone because of that.

66
00:08:03,348 --> 00:08:21,696
So in other words, one attribute of a fully liberated person is that instead of being angry or despising somebody who can't keep the rules or isn't well behaved, instead he would look upon them with compassion.

67
00:08:22,297 --> 00:08:25,541
They are spiritually sick.

68
00:08:29,233 --> 00:08:33,379
Now he should question the Tathagata even further.

69
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:43,693
So now what we have is a passage where this is repeated and the Buddha now replies on his own behalf.

70
00:08:44,195 --> 00:08:50,923
There are no defiled states cognizable through the eye or through the ear found in the Tathagata.

71
00:08:51,544 --> 00:08:56,371
There are no mixed states cognizable through the eye or through the ear

72
00:08:56,756 --> 00:08:58,259
found in the Tathagata.

73
00:08:58,278 --> 00:09:01,123
In other words, one minute is good and the next minute is bad.

74
00:09:03,966 --> 00:09:11,777
Now, are there found in the Tathagata or not cleansed states cognizable through the eye, through the ear?

75
00:09:12,437 --> 00:09:14,159
Yes, there are, the Buddha replies.

76
00:09:14,581 --> 00:09:21,971
They are my pathway and my domain, yet I do not identify with them.

77
00:09:22,491 --> 00:09:26,476
That's a clear point of non-identification with

78
00:09:26,962 --> 00:09:32,529
those beautiful virtues of compassion, love, sympathetic joy, etc.

79
00:09:36,374 --> 00:09:40,960
A disciple should approach the teacher who speaks to us in order to hear the Dharma.

80
00:09:41,701 --> 00:09:52,953
The teacher teaches him the Dharma with its higher and higher levels, with its more and more sublime levels, with its dark and bright counterparts.

81
